<text top="89" left="420" width="82" height="11" font="1"><b>SECOND DAY </b></text>
<text top="103" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="117" left="194" width="139" height="11" font="1"><b>Tuesday, October 29, 2013 </b></text>
<text top="130" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="144" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  The House of Representatives of the Twenty-Seventh Legislature of the </text>
<text top="158" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">State  of  Hawaii,  Second  Special  Session  of  2013,  convened  at  10:10 </text>
<text top="172" left="81" width="61" height="11" font="0">o'clock a.m.,</text>
<text top="172" left="142" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="172" left="145" width="147" height="11" font="0">with Speaker Souki presiding. </text>
<text top="186" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="199" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  The  invocation  was  delivered  by  Representative  Justin  H.  Woodson, </text>
<text top="213" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">after  which  the  Roll  was  called  showing  all  Members  present  with  the </text>
<text top="227" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">exception  of  Representatives  Carroll,  Choy,  Kobayashi,  Nakashima  and </text>
<text top="241" left="81" width="141" height="11" font="0">Yamane, who were excused. </text>
<text top="255" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="268" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  By unanimous consent, reading and approval of the Journal of the House </text>
<text top="282" left="81" width="238" height="11" font="0">of Representatives of the First Day was deferred. </text>
<text top="296" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="310" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="324" left="210" width="106" height="11" font="1"><b>INTRODUCTIONS </b></text>
<text top="337" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="351" left="81" width="340" height="11" font="0">  The following introduction was made to the Members of the House: </text>
<text top="365" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="379" left="81" width="350" height="11" font="0">  Representative Oshiro introduced his former teacher, Ms. Sally Waitt. </text>
<text top="393" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="406" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="420" left="202" width="123" height="11" font="1"><b>ORDER OF THE DAY </b></text>
<text top="434" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="448" left="147" width="233" height="11" font="1"><b>REPORTS OF STANDING COMMITTEES </b></text>
<text top="462" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="475" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  Representatives  Nakashima  and  Luke,  for  the  Committee  on  Labor  &amp; </text>
<text top="489" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">Public  Employment  and  the  Committee  on  Finance,  presented  a  report </text>
<text top="503" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">(Stand.  Com.  Rep.  No.  1)  recommending  that  H.B.  No.  1  pass  Second </text>
<text top="517" left="81" width="281" height="11" font="0">Reading and be placed on the calendar for Third Reading. </text>
<text top="531" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="544" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  On motion by Representative Saiki, seconded by Representative Mizuno </text>
<text top="558" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">and  carried,  the  report  of  the  Committees  was  adopted  and  H.B.  No.  1, </text>
<text top="572" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">entitled:    &#34;A  BILL  FOR  AN  ACT  MAKING  APPROPRIATIONS  FOR </text>
<text top="586" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">COLLECTIVE  BARGAINING  COST  ITEMS,&#34;  passed  Second  Reading </text>
<text top="600" left="81" width="364" height="11" font="0">and  was  placed  on  the  calendar  for  Third  Reading,  with  Representatives </text>
<text top="613" left="81" width="324" height="11" font="0">Carroll, Choy, Kobayashi, Nakashima and Yamane being excused. </text>
<text top="627" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="641" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  Representatives  Nakashima  and  Luke,  for  the  Committee  on  Labor  &amp; </text>
<text top="655" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">Public  Employment  and  the  Committee  on  Finance,  presented  a  report </text>
<text top="669" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">(Stand.  Com.  Rep.  No.  2)  recommending  that  H.B.  No.  2  pass  Second </text>
<text top="682" left="81" width="281" height="11" font="0">Reading and be placed on the calendar for Third Reading. </text>
<text top="696" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="710" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  On motion by Representative Saiki, seconded by Representative Mizuno </text>
<text top="724" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">and  carried,  the  report  of  the  Committees  was  adopted  and  H.B.  No.  2, </text>
<text top="738" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">entitled:    &#34;A  BILL  FOR  AN  ACT  MAKING  APPROPRIATIONS  FOR </text>
<text top="751" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">COLLECTIVE  BARGAINING  COST  ITEMS,&#34;  passed  Second  Reading </text>
<text top="765" left="81" width="364" height="11" font="0">and  was  placed  on  the  calendar  for  Third  Reading,  with  Representatives </text>
<text top="779" left="81" width="324" height="11" font="0">Carroll, Choy, Kobayashi, Nakashima and Yamane being excused. </text>
<text top="793" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="807" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  Representatives Belatti and Luke, for the Committee on  Health and the </text>
<text top="820" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">Committee  on  Finance,  presented  a  report  (Stand.  Com.  Rep.  No.  3) </text>
<text top="834" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">recommending that H.B. No. 3, as amended in HD 1, pass Second Reading </text>
<text top="848" left="81" width="238" height="11" font="0">and be placed on the calendar for Third Reading. </text>
<text top="862" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="876" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  On motion by Representative Saiki, seconded by Representative Mizuno </text>
<text top="889" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">and  carried,  the  report  of  the  Committees  was  adopted  and  H.B.  No.  3, </text>
<text top="903" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">HD 1,  entitled:    &#34;A  BILL  FOR  AN  ACT  MAKING  AN </text>
<text top="917" left="81" width="97" height="11" font="0">APPROPRIATION </text>
<text top="917" left="192" width="19" height="11" font="0">TO </text>
<text top="917" left="224" width="27" height="11" font="0">THE </text>
<text top="917" left="263" width="48" height="11" font="0">HAWAII </text>
<text top="917" left="325" width="51" height="11" font="0">HEALTH </text>
<text top="917" left="389" width="57" height="11" font="0">SYSTEMS </text>
<text top="931" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">CORPORATION,&#34;  passed  Second  Reading  and  was  placed  on  the </text>
<text top="945" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">calendar  for  Third  Reading,  with  Representatives  Carroll,  Choy, </text>
<text top="959" left="81" width="252" height="11" font="0">Kobayashi, Nakashima and Yamane being excused. </text>
<text top="972" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="986" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="1000" left="185" width="157" height="11" font="1"><b>INTRODUCTION OF BILLS </b></text>
<text top="1014" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="1027" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">  On  motion  by  Representative  Saiki,  seconded  by  Representative </text>
<text top="1041" left="81" width="365" height="11" font="0">Johanson and carried, the following bills (H.B. Nos. 6 through 12) passed </text>
<text top="1055" left="81" width="364" height="11" font="0">First  Reading  by  title  and  were  referred  to  Printing:    (Representatives </text>
<text top="1069" left="81" width="325" height="11" font="0">Carroll, Choy, Kobayashi, Nakashima and Yamane were excused.) </text>
<text top="1083" left="81" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="117" left="475" width="55" height="11" font="1"><b>H. B. Nos. </b></text>
<text top="131" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="144" left="475" width="9" height="11" font="0">6 </text>
<text top="144" left="529" width="308" height="11" font="0">&#34;A BILL FOR AN ACT RELATING TO CIVIL LIBERTIES.&#34; </text>
<text top="158" left="529" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="172" left="529" width="73" height="11" font="0">Introduced by: </text>
<text top="172" left="637" width="112" height="11" font="0">Representative Jordan. </text>
<text top="200" left="475" width="9" height="11" font="0">7 </text>
<text top="200" left="529" width="312" height="11" font="0">&#34;A  BILL  FOR  AN  ACT  RELATING  TO  PERSONAL </text>
<text top="213" left="529" width="104" height="11" font="0">RELATIONSHIPS.&#34; </text>
<text top="227" left="529" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="241" left="529" width="73" height="11" font="0">Introduced by: </text>
<text top="241" left="637" width="79" height="11" font="0">Representatives </text>
<text top="241" left="730" width="57" height="11" font="0">McKelvey, </text>
<text top="241" left="801" width="40" height="11" font="0">Carroll, </text>
<text top="255" left="529" width="111" height="11" font="0">Evans and Kawakami. </text>
<text top="283" left="475" width="9" height="11" font="0">8 </text>
<text top="283" left="529" width="312" height="11" font="0">&#34;A BILL FOR AN ACT PROPOSING AN AMENDMENT TO </text>
<text top="296" left="529" width="312" height="11" font="0">THE  HAWAII  CONSTITUTION  TO  DEFINE  MARRIAGE </text>
<text top="310" left="529" width="311" height="11" font="0">AS  THE  LAWFUL  UNION  OF  ONE  MAN  AND  ONE </text>
<text top="324" left="529" width="59" height="11" font="0">WOMAN.&#34; </text>
<text top="338" left="529" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="352" left="529" width="73" height="11" font="0">Introduced by: </text>
<text top="352" left="637" width="101" height="11" font="0">Representative Fale. </text>
<text top="380" left="475" width="9" height="11" font="0">9 </text>
<text top="380" left="529" width="16" height="11" font="0">&#34;A </text>
<text top="380" left="558" width="30" height="11" font="0">BILL </text>
<text top="380" left="599" width="26" height="11" font="0">FOR </text>
<text top="380" left="638" width="20" height="11" font="0">AN </text>
<text top="380" left="670" width="27" height="11" font="0">ACT </text>
<text top="380" left="709" width="63" height="11" font="0">RELATING </text>
<text top="380" left="784" width="19" height="11" font="0">TO </text>
<text top="380" left="815" width="26" height="11" font="0">THE </text>
<text top="393" left="529" width="311" height="11" font="0">DEPARTMENT  OF  EDUCATION'S  SCHOOL  FOOD </text>
<text top="407" left="529" width="130" height="11" font="0">SERVICES PROGRAM.&#34; </text>
<text top="421" left="529" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="435" left="529" width="73" height="11" font="0">Introduced by: </text>
<text top="435" left="637" width="101" height="11" font="0">Representative Fale. </text>
<text top="463" left="475" width="15" height="11" font="0">10 </text>
<text top="463" left="529" width="312" height="11" font="0">&#34;A  BILL  FOR  AN  ACT  RELATING  TO  CAPITAL </text>
<text top="476" left="529" width="311" height="11" font="0">IMPROVEMENT  PROJECTS  FOR  THE  BENEFIT  OF  THE </text>
<text top="490" left="529" width="183" height="11" font="0">DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATION.&#34; </text>
<text top="504" left="529" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="518" left="529" width="73" height="11" font="0">Introduced by: </text>
<text top="518" left="637" width="98" height="11" font="0">Representative Har. </text>
<text top="546" left="475" width="15" height="11" font="0">11 </text>
<text top="546" left="529" width="312" height="11" font="0">&#34;A  BILL  FOR  AN  ACT  RELATING  TO  SEXUALITY </text>
<text top="559" left="529" width="132" height="11" font="0">HEALTH EDUCATION.&#34; </text>
<text top="573" left="529" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="587" left="529" width="73" height="11" font="0">Introduced by: </text>
<text top="587" left="637" width="204" height="11" font="0">Representatives  Ward,  Fale,  Fukumoto </text>
<text top="601" left="529" width="82" height="11" font="0">and McDermott. </text>
<text top="628" left="475" width="15" height="11" font="0">12 </text>
<text top="628" left="529" width="312" height="11" font="0">&#34;A  BILL  FOR  AN  ACT  RELATING  TO  RELIGIOUS </text>
<text top="642" left="529" width="62" height="11" font="0">LIBERTY.&#34; </text>
<text top="656" left="529" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="670" left="529" width="73" height="11" font="0">Introduced by: </text>
<text top="670" left="637" width="204" height="11" font="0">Representatives  Ward,  Fale,  Fukumoto </text>
<text top="684" left="529" width="82" height="11" font="0">and McDermott. </text>
<text top="712" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="726" left="553" width="208" height="11" font="1"><b>INTRODUCTION OF RESOLUTIONS </b></text>
<text top="739" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="753" left="475" width="365" height="11" font="0">  The following resolution (H.R. No. 1) was announced by the Clerk and </text>
<text top="767" left="475" width="132" height="11" font="0">the following action taken: </text>
<text top="781" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="794" left="475" width="365" height="11" font="0">  H.R.  No.  1,  entitled:    &#34;HOUSE  RESOLUTION  RELATING  TO  THE </text>
<text top="808" left="475" width="365" height="11" font="0">CAUCUS  LEADERS  AND  THE  COMMITTEE  ASSIGNMENTS  OF </text>
<text top="822" left="475" width="365" height="11" font="0">THE  HOUSE  OF  REPRESENTATIVES OF  THE  TWENTY-SEVENTH </text>
<text top="836" left="475" width="362" height="11" font="0">LEGISLATURE,&#34; was jointly offered by Representatives Souki and Saiki. </text>
<text top="850" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="863" left="475" width="365" height="11" font="0">  Representative  Saiki  moved  that  H.R.  No.  1  be  adopted,  seconded  by </text>
<text top="877" left="475" width="125" height="11" font="0">Representative Johanson. </text>
<text top="891" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="905" left="475" width="364" height="11" font="0">  At  10:18  o'clock  a.m.,  Representative  Saiki  requested  a  recess  and  the </text>
<text top="919" left="475" width="265" height="11" font="0">Chair declared a recess subject to the call of the Chair. </text>
<text top="932" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="946" left="475" width="319" height="11" font="0">  The House of Representatives reconvened at 11:58 o'clock a.m. </text>
<text top="960" left="475" width="3" height="9" font="3"> </text>
<text top="972" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="986" left="475" width="365" height="11" font="0">  The motion was put to vote by the Chair and carried, and H.R. No. 1 was </text>
<text top="1000" left="475" width="365" height="11" font="0">adopted,  with  Representatives  Choy,  Nakashima,  Tokioka  and  Yamane </text>
<text top="1013" left="475" width="74" height="11" font="0">being excused. </text>
<text top="1027" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="1"><b> </b></text>
<text top="1041" left="475" width="364" height="11" font="0">  At  11:59  o'clock  a.m.,  Representative  Saiki  requested  a  recess  and  the </text>
<text top="1055" left="475" width="265" height="11" font="0">Chair declared a recess subject to the call of the Chair. </text>
<text top="1069" left="475" width="3" height="11" font="0"> </text>
<text top="1083" left="475" width="320" height="11" font="0">  The House of Representatives reconvened at 12:02 o'clock p.m. </text>
<text top="1094" left="475" width="1" height="3" font="4"> </text>
<text top="1098" left="475" width="1" height="3" font="4"> </text>
